    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2CkNuSJrjB76ZiHYGn2MXpt)_\n\n## What\n\n- New command `M-x sp-see-also-show-concept-by-name` next to `sp-see-also-show-concept`.\n- It prompts in the minibuffer for a note by title, so no ID is typed and the entry at point is not used.\n- It then opens the same `*see-also-concept*` view (code reused as is).\n- The prompt is `sp-select-note` with the new `:grouped t` option: the groups of `sp-find-note` (notes, writing projects, config), with the tag emoji and column.\n- `:require-match t`, so the choice always exists.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `sp-org-tag-groups`: the grouping `let` of `sp-find-note` is now the macro `sp-org-tag-groups--with-origin-groups`; `sp-find-note` behaves as before.\n- `sp-select-note` gets `:grouped`.\n- Literate docs updated (bullet lists) and re-tangled; `tools/check-tangle.sh` matches.\n- Test added; the 28 `sp-see-also` tests pass in Emacs 29.3.\n\n## Not done\n\n- Not run in the real GUI or against the real vault.\n- No keybinding yet.\n- Branch is not number-prefixed (rename is blocked here); no `CHANGELOG.org` edit, per the rules.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi8hmjgGyhMeZ9AvbZU)_",
